<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE reference
  PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450385" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 6 — Table embedded inside a list item</title>
   <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>inside</keyword>
        <keyword>table</keyword>
        <keyword>element</keyword>
        <keyword>Table</keyword>
        <keyword>embedded</keyword>
        <keyword>HTML</keyword>
        <indexterm>inside</indexterm>
        <indexterm>table</indexterm>
        <indexterm>element</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d611e7">
         <p>Consider a <codeph>&lt;ul&gt;</codeph> list where the author has inserted a <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> element directly inside one of the <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> items — for example, to present a small reference table as part of a bullet point.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Table embedded in list item</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_izv_f44_lkc">
&lt;ul>
  &lt;li>
    The following options are available:
    &lt;table>
      &lt;tr>
        &lt;th>Option&lt;/th>
        &lt;th>Default&lt;/th>
      &lt;/tr>
      &lt;tr>
        &lt;td>Retry&lt;/td>
        &lt;td>3 times&lt;/td>
      &lt;/tr>
      &lt;tr>
        &lt;td>Timeout&lt;/td>
        &lt;td>30 sec&lt;/td>
      &lt;/tr>
    &lt;/table>
  &lt;/li>
&lt;/ul></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                   
                     
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_oqg_344_lkc">
&lt;conbody>
  &lt;ul>
    &lt;li>
      The following options are available:
      &lt;simpletable>
        &lt;sthead>
          &lt;stentry>Option&lt;/stentry>
          &lt;stentry>Default&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;/sthead>
        &lt;strow>
          &lt;stentry>Retry&lt;/stentry>
          &lt;stentry>3 times&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;/strow>
        &lt;strow>
          &lt;stentry>Timeout&lt;/stentry>
          &lt;stentry>30 sec&lt;/stentry>
        &lt;/strow>
      &lt;/simpletable>
    &lt;/li>
  &lt;/ul>
&lt;/conbody></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p>
            <b>Result:</b> When a <codeph>&lt;table&gt;</codeph> element is correctly nested inside an <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> element in the HTML source, the converter maps it to a <codeph>&lt;simpletable&gt;</codeph> inside the corresponding DITA <codeph>&lt;li&gt;</codeph> element. Always verify that the table-inside-list structure is preserved correctly in the HTML source before conversion.</p>
      </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
